## 3. Mapping OOP Concepts to Implementation

| OOP Concept | Project Application | Why It Matters for Interviews |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Classes & Objects** | Concrete instances of `Rider`, `Driver`, `Car`, `Ride`, `Payment`. | Demonstrates ability to model real-world domains cleanly in code. |
| **Encapsulation** | Private attributes (e.g. `isAvailable`, `currentRideId`, `fare`) exposed only through validated accessors and state-modifying methods. | Prevents illegal state tampering (e.g. directly setting a ride to completed without calculating fare). |
| **Inheritance** | `User` → `Rider`, `Driver`<br>`Vehicle` → `Car`, `Bike`, `Auto` | Promotes code reuse; avoids duplicating `name`, `phone`, `licensePlate` across subclasses. |
| **Abstraction** | Abstract base class `Vehicle` with pure virtual function `getType() = 0` and virtual `calculateFare()`. | High-level systems (e.g. `Ride`) don't need to know vehicle mechanics—they just ask for the fare. |
| **Polymorphism** | Calling `vehicle->calculateFare(distance)` dynamically executes the derived class algorithm (`Car`, `Bike`, or `Auto`) through a base pointer/reference. | Demonstrates runtime dispatch (vtable mechanism) in C++. |
| **Constructors & Initializer Lists** | Member initializer lists used everywhere (e.g., `Car(...) : Vehicle(...) {}`). | Modern C++ best practice, avoids default-construction overhead. |
| **Composition & Association** | - `Driver` owns a `Vehicle` (Composition via `std::unique_ptr`).<br>- `Ride` references `Rider` and `Driver` by IDs (Association). | Demonstrates understanding of object lifecycles and avoiding memory leaks or cyclic references. |
| **STL Containers** | `std::vector` for histories, `std::unordered_map` for O(1) entity lookups by ID. | Demonstrates practical standard library mastery over raw C arrays. |
| **Exception Handling** | Throwing `std::invalid_argument` (negative distance, invalid phone) and custom `RideException` (driver already busy, illegal state jump). | Robust error handling without crashing the CLI process. |
| **File Handling** | Serializing/deserializing riders, drivers, and ride logs using `std::ifstream`, `std::ofstream`, and `std::stringstream`. | Shows persistent storage without bloated external database drivers. |

