## 6. Data Storage & Persistence Strategy

### 6.1 In-Memory Management
- The system operates smoothly using `std::unordered_map` and `std::vector` inside `RideManager`.
- Ensures that logic, state transitions, and OOP hierarchies remain decoupled from storage.

### 6.2 Lightweight CSV Persistence
- CSV (Comma-Separated Values) files stored in `data/`:
  - `riders.csv`: `id,name,phone`
  - `drivers.csv`: `id,name,phone,vehicleType,licensePlate,isAvailable`
  - `rides.csv`: `rideId,riderId,driverId,pickup,drop,distance,vehicleType,status,fare`
- Read/Write logic handled using clean C++ streams (`std::ifstream`, `std::ofstream`, `std::stringstream`).

