## 8. Project Sizing & Scope Guardrails

- **Target Duration:** 1 to 2 weeks for a 2nd-year B.Tech student working at a steady pace.
- **Code Size:** ~700–900 lines of total, well-documented C++ code across all files.
- **Maintainability:** Every file has a single, well-defined responsibility (< 100 lines per file on average).
- **Interview Readiness:** Every OOP concept used directly answers common C++ interview questions (e.g., *"Why is the destructor virtual in the base class?"*, *"What is the difference between composition and inheritance?"*, *"How does runtime polymorphism work via virtual functions?"*).

